{{inh+|es|osp|filo}}, inherited from {{inh|es|la|fīlum}}. {{dbt|es|hilo}}. Both were inherited, and it is not entirely clear why the two diverged in pronunciation, with ''filo'' coming to mean 'edge' and ''hilo'' maintaining the Latin sense of 'string, thread'. Perhaps the /f~h/ variation was exploited to create two words with more specialized senses.

